0..76 Comment "// This record type has a face poset wider than one machine word. Its twelve"
77..154 Comment "// faces lie over nine labels. Their 66 pairwise meets differ from each other"
155..231 Comment "// and from each face. So the poset holds 78 cells. A system over two of the"
232..248 Comment "// faces checks."
249..251 Comment "//"
252..329 Comment "// A face poset holds a record type\'s faces and each new meet of two faces. A"
330..408 Comment "// system converts each later face on its meet with the first face. Faces that"
409..484 Comment "// overlap at different labels give one meet for each pair. So twelve faces"
485..502 Comment "// pass 64 cells."
503..505 Comment "//"
506..580 Comment "// The order of the face poset keeps one row of words for each cell. A row"
581..660 Comment "// keeps one word for each 64 cells. These 78 cells keep two words in each row."
661..737 Comment "// The lowering states the most cells a face poset holds. A record type past"
738..775 Comment "// that count is refused by its name."
776..778 Comment "//"
779..827 Comment "// - see: #5668 — the face poset past 64 cells"
828..905 Comment "// - see: `model/desc/record-faces.gandr` — a record type\'s faces, a static"
906..965 Comment "//   bracket by label or by face, and a system of two faces"
966..1042 Comment "// - see: `pathological/desc/record-faces.gandr` — the faces a record type"
1043..1055 Comment "//   refuses"
1057..1132 Comment "/// A deployment: twelve faces, each over five to seven of its nine labels."
1133..1211 Comment "/// The faces `placed` and `served` meet at the port, the region, the zone and"
1212..1229 Comment "/// the replicas."
